tial ran 213 inputs with 0 differences, but its harness stubs setActiveMenu, so it says nothing about Back.\n\n**Questions for a human.** (1) Back after a deeper search result (KI, reproduced). (2) A removed parent menu applies a stale index to root. (3) The PR's extraction regex throws when a comment sits above goBack.\n\n**Traceability.** setActiveMenu is traced to DE93 and B4CK. 35 requirements are code_changed through file-level traces only. unmapped_code and the 11 spec-gap candidates are all our PoC (pocs/**, production_exclude). Change effects were not analyzed. The KI's introduced_in (2c06591a) is this mirror's apply commit.\n\n**Not caused by this PR.** test_outcome_unobserved:SW-REQ-260929-B8N9 is an engine artefact: item() at Menu.qml:233 is read as a test (name starts with 'it'). It is a witness at the base too. It still prevents readiness. No gate fails."}
